 r←Test_POSTRefresh_PendingRuns url;Assert;first;state
⍝ Check a queued refresh actually runs once the current one finishes.
⍝ started_at is re-stamped at the top of every cycle, so a change proves a second
⍝ cycle ran, whether the second trigger queued or started its own build after the first.
 r←0
 Assert←##.Assert
 state←#.DCMS.GLOBAL.refresh
 :Trap 0
     'Refresh already running at start of test'Assert ##.WaitRefreshIdle 150
     {}('POST'Authed url,'/admin/refresh').Run
     first←state.started_at
     {}('POST'Authed url,'/admin/refresh').Run
     'Refresh did not return to idle'Assert ##.WaitRefreshIdle 300
     'Second refresh cycle never ran'Assert first≢state.started_at
     'Pending flag not cleared'Assert 0=state.pending
     r←1
 :EndTrap
⍝ Teardown: never leak a refresh worker into the next test
 {}##.WaitRefreshIdle 300
